  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Credit Ratings Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Private sector investment as well as the business environment in Africa are constricted by a low volume of funding and the high cost of borrowing. With the decline of Official Development Assistance (ODA) from 68% of financial inflows in 1900 to the continent to less than 25% by 2022, more African countries are turning to global capital markets to obtain financing for development. Over the next decade, African countries must finance critical investments, with annual estimates around $100 billion</narrative>
  </description>
